codex
Findings:

High: `evaluate_hypothetical_order` is not read-only. It builds an unsaved proposal, then calls `Guardrails::Evaluator` [app/models/agent/tools/evaluate_hypothetical_order.rb](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/app/models/agent/tools/evaluate_hypothetical_order.rb:15). The evaluator can call `trip_rule_halt!` through daily loss/drawdown rules [daily_loss_halt.rb](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/app/models/guardrails/daily_loss_halt.rb:9), [max_drawdown_halt.rb](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/app/models/guardrails/max_drawdown_halt.rb:9), writing `system_settings` and audit rows. This must change before commit: add a non-mutating evaluator mode or move halt writes out of dry-run evaluation.

High: missing hard-rule rows fail open. `Evaluator` returns `unavailable` for every missing rule except `settled_cash` [evaluator.rb](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/app/models/guardrails/evaluator.rb:18), and `Report#blocked?` only treats `fail` as blocking [guardrails.rb](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/app/models/guardrails.rb:15). A missing `max_risk_per_trade`, `notional_cap`, or `stop_collar` row can validate with acknowledgement. Rules 1-4 and 7 hard failures, plus missing/bad collar data, should hard-fail before commit.

High: rule halt reset math is wrong. An indefinite drawdown halt can be shortened by a later finite halt because `[rule_halt_resets_at, resets_at].compact.max` drops `nil` [system_settings.rb](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/app/models/system_settings.rb:18). Daily loss also resets at end of day [daily_loss_halt.rb](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/app/models/guardrails/daily_loss_halt.rb:9), while the code comment and intended behavior say tomorrow’s open. Fix before commit.

High: approval re-evaluation will not catch equity/rule deterioration. `MaxRiskPerTrade` compares risk against the frozen `sizing["risk_budget"]` [max_risk_per_trade.rb](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/app/models/guardrails/max_risk_per_trade.rb:8), not current fresh equity times the active rule. If equity halves after proposal creation, the frozen quantity can still pass. Must change before commit.

Medium: settled cash double-reserves the same submitted buy once it has synced as a live broker order: app proposals [context.rb](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/app/models/guardrails/context.rb:25) plus live broker buys [context.rb](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/app/models/guardrails/context.rb:29). If intentional, add a spec and surface it clearly; otherwise exclude linked orders before commit.

Medium: exit proposals can be hard-blocked by `notional_cap` because it has no `entry?` guard [notional_cap.rb](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/app/models/guardrails/notional_cap.rb:3). That conflicts with the “exits stay available” safety intent unless exits have a separate held-quantity/fat-finger rule. Decide before commit, not step 3.

Medium: collar quality/config is incomplete for step 2. The calculator always computes all methods and lacks method on/off config [calculator.rb](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/app/models/stop_collar/calculator.rb:24), despite PRD configuration requiring method enablement. Its candle freshness is `4.days`, not “latest within two trading days” via `MarketDay` [calculator.rb](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/app/models/stop_collar/calculator.rb:7). Fix before commit. I did not see stale cached history pass once marked `stale`; that gate exists.

Wash-sale lot precision can wait only if explicitly scoped: sell loss detection uses average entry [wash_sale.rb](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/app/models/guardrails/wash_sale.rb:14), not FIFO/tax lots, so it can miss actual loss sales. Step 2 includes wash-sale correctness, so I would fix or hard-label this limitation before commit.
